<title>UK: Rolls Royce wins 13 mln stg Turkish contract.</title>
<headline>Rolls Royce wins 13 mln stg Turkish contract.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>British engineering group Rolls-Royce Plc said on Wednesday that it has won a 13 million stg contract for a port development in Turkey.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that Caillard, part of its materials handling division, will extend a coal and iron ore terminal for Turkish steel company Eregli Iron and Steel Works (Erdemir).</p>
<p>Caillard will supply two 1,500 tonnes per hour free digging capacity coal and ore grab unloaders, five conveyors with a total length of 1.8 km, and five transfer towers.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
